\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\title{Union and intersection notation}
\taxon{Remark}
\p{The notation for intersection and union is not an accident. Notice that #{\cap} is defined in terms of #{\land} and #{\cup} is defined in terms of #{\lor}; intersection is kind of like “AND for sets” and union is “OR for sets”. (Also #{\cup} looks like a “U” for “union”.)}
